hash-chain-build:
Longest consecutive chain — START ONLY AT CHAIN HEADS:

  arr = [100, 4, 200, 1, 3, 2]
  set = {100, 4, 200, 1, 3, 2}

  for x in set:
    if (x-1) in set: skip (not a head)
    else: walk x, x+1, x+2, ... ← only fires at TRUE heads

  1 is a head (0 ∉ set) → walk 1,2,3,4 → length 4 ✓
  100 is a head → walk 100 → length 1
  200 is a head → walk 200 → length 1
